00:00:00.649 --> 00:00:06.670
Hello and welcome to this video in which we will
look at what a workplace audit is and how to carry

00:00:06.670 --> 00:00:09.620
out a workplace audit using the 5S methodology.

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:15.739
A key method of maximizing the safety
and efficiency of a workplace is to

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:18.059
score and conduct a workplace audit.

00:00:18.855 --> 00:00:22.955
So what exactly is a workplace
audit, and how does scoring work?

00:00:23.495 --> 00:00:25.395
Let's take a look at this in more detail.

00:00:26.175 --> 00:00:31.275
A workplace organization, audit is a
systematic evaluation of the cleanliness,

00:00:31.704 --> 00:00:34.864
organization, and efficiency of a workplace.

00:00:35.415 --> 00:00:40.335
The purpose of an audit is to identify areas
for improvement, and to ensure that the

00:00:40.335 --> 00:00:43.055
workplace is operating safely and efficiently.

00:00:44.404 --> 00:00:47.095
So what are the steps
involved in a workplace audit?

00:00:47.835 --> 00:00:52.835
The first step in auditing a workplace
organization is to develop a scoring system.

00:00:53.374 --> 00:00:58.175
This involves determining the criteria that
will be used to evaluate the workplace.

00:00:58.940 --> 00:01:03.970
Once the criteria have been determined,
you can then assign a numerical value to

00:01:03.970 --> 00:01:06.830
each criterion to create a scoring system.

00:01:07.390 --> 00:01:11.920
This can then be incorporated into an
audit checklist, and the scores from

00:01:11.929 --> 00:01:16.520
each aspect are then combined to give
an overall score for the workplace.

00:01:17.234 --> 00:01:21.455
These scores are then used to determine
the overall performance of the workplace

00:01:21.845 --> 00:01:24.195
and to identify areas for improvement.

00:01:24.744 --> 00:01:30.514
The scores can be compared to previous audits or
to industry standards to determine whether the

00:01:30.514 --> 00:01:34.004
workplace is performing well or needs improvement.

00:01:35.255 --> 00:01:40.795
In the context of auditing and scoring
workplace organization, the 5S methodology

00:01:40.795 --> 00:01:45.804
can be used as a tool for assessing the level
of workplace organization and cleanliness.

00:01:46.524 --> 00:01:48.435
Let's take a look at how this can be done.

00:01:49.185 --> 00:01:50.805
The first step is preparation.

00:01:51.225 --> 00:01:57.205
Review the 5S principles and gather any
relevant documentation and data that relates

00:01:57.205 --> 00:02:04.025
to the area being audited, such as standard
operating procedures, process maps, the number

00:02:04.025 --> 00:02:09.824
of accidents, the amount of waste generated,
and the time it takes to complete tasks.

00:02:10.410 --> 00:02:14.890
This data will be used to support the
observations made during the visual inspection.

00:02:15.640 --> 00:02:19.430
Once you have all the relevant
documentation, you can then begin the audit.

00:02:21.310 --> 00:02:23.830
The first 5S step in the audit is sort.

00:02:24.290 --> 00:02:29.019
This is where you evaluate the physical
organization of the workplace, including the

00:02:29.020 --> 00:02:31.730
storage of items and the placement of equipment.

00:02:32.270 --> 00:02:36.620
In this step, you are identifying
what is needed and what is not needed.

00:02:37.160 --> 00:02:41.799
All of the items that you believe are
not required should be read tagged and

00:02:41.799 --> 00:02:44.060
moved to a holding area for evaluation.

00:02:45.310 --> 00:02:48.280
After sorting, the next step is set in order.

00:02:48.860 --> 00:02:53.739
Put simply, this means arranging things
so they are easy to find and use.

00:02:54.305 --> 00:02:59.875
Once all the clutter has been removed, this
step is about organizing the remaining items

00:02:59.875 --> 00:03:02.084
in a way that is intuitive and efficient.

00:03:02.635 --> 00:03:08.244
This may involve creating designated
storage areas, labeling items, or

00:03:08.245 --> 00:03:12.845
establishing clear visual cues for where
tools and materials should be kept.

00:03:14.685 --> 00:03:20.715
Once items are set in order, the next step is
shine, which simply means to keep the workplace

00:03:20.734 --> 00:03:23.204
clean and organized with good maintenance.

00:03:23.785 --> 00:03:30.355
In this step, the workspace is cleaned thoroughly
and any remaining dirt or debris is removed.

00:03:30.895 --> 00:03:34.874
Regular cleaning should take place
as it is important to maintain a safe

00:03:35.125 --> 00:03:37.105
and sanitary working environment.

00:03:38.965 --> 00:03:42.044
Step 4 of the audit process is standardize.

00:03:42.824 --> 00:03:49.524
This step is all about developing and implementing
standard operating procedures to control and keep

00:03:49.545 --> 00:03:52.215
the workplace clean and organized all of the time.

00:03:52.920 --> 00:03:57.760
This may involve creating checklists,
documenting procedures, and training

00:03:57.760 --> 00:03:59.670
employees on the new processes.

00:04:01.530 --> 00:04:05.010
The fifth and final step in
the audit process is sustain.

00:04:05.770 --> 00:04:11.630
This final step involves ensuring that the new
processes and standards are maintained over time.

00:04:12.199 --> 00:04:18.090
This may involve regularly reviewing and auditing
the workspace, providing ongoing training and

00:04:18.090 --> 00:04:25.410
support to employees, and continuously improving
processes based on feedback and new ideas.

00:04:25.420 --> 00:04:31.890
Thank you Now that you have learnt about
each of the steps involved in a 5S audit,

00:04:32.300 --> 00:04:36.380
let's take a look at the audit checklist,
as you will be required to carry out

00:04:36.380 --> 00:04:38.330
an audit as part of your assessment.

00:04:38.890 --> 00:04:44.620
You can see the checklist contains a section
for each of the 5SAs with a number of questions.

00:04:45.189 --> 00:04:49.109
This next image shows an office
before an audit has taken place.

00:04:49.690 --> 00:04:51.870
As you can see it is in a bit of a mess.

00:04:52.455 --> 00:04:58.335
The person carrying out the audit works through
each section and gives each question a score

00:04:58.335 --> 00:05:03.344
based on what is seen and makes comments about
what actions are required for improvement.

00:05:03.914 --> 00:05:06.265
Clearly, this room wouldn't score very highly.

00:05:06.794 --> 00:05:10.145
Once the audit is complete, the
remedial actions should be carried

00:05:10.145 --> 00:05:12.455
out and another audit take place.

00:05:13.030 --> 00:05:16.440
This second audit should see a
marked improvement over the first.

00:05:17.039 --> 00:05:21.309
Further audits should be carried out
periodically to ensure that the AA is fully

00:05:21.309 --> 00:05:24.179
compliant and maintains this compliance.

